messages.content:
value is [numbers, width]. Return averages of every full contiguous window of width. Return [] when width > len(numbers). Raise ValueError for width <= 0. Inputs are integers; output may be float.
Implement solve(value), taking one JSON array argument, without mutating that argument. Return only the complete replacement file in exactly one fenced python block.


Current solution.py:
```python
def solve(value):
    a, width = value
    return [sum(a[i:i+width]) / width for i in range(len(a)-width)]
```

